    "texte": [
      "Over the past half-century, human societies have undergone a structural metamorphosis whose velocity and breadth have scarcely any precedent in recorded history. Where earlier epochs experienced change across the span of several generations—allowing cultural norms, moral frameworks, and social hierarchies to adapt organically—contemporary societies are defined by perpetual acceleration. The convergence of digital hyper-connectivity, globalized financial markets, demographic shifts, and ecological disruption has dismantled the predictable life trajectories that once anchored industrial modernity. As the sociologist Zygmunt Bauman famously observed in his characterization of 'liquid modernity,' institutions, professional identities, and social allegiances have lost their former solidity, dissolving into fluid arrangements that demand constant reinvention from the individual.",
