      "The most conspicuous feature of this transformation is the steady eastward and southward migration of global economic weight. Emerging economies across Asia, Latin America, and Africa now account for the majority of global growth, demographic expansion, and demand for critical minerals and digital infrastructure. Simultaneously, the strategic rivalry between major economic blocs has prompted governments to replace blind faith in laissez-faire markets with activist industrial policies: subsidies for semiconductors, clean-technology manufacturing, and domestic battery production have become central instruments of national security.",
