"When a routine software update recently triggered a global cloud outage, airports ground to a halt, hospital surgeries were postponed, payment terminals froze across supermarkets, and millions of commuters stared helplessly at blank transit screens. Watching this cascading paralysis unfold from my newsroom desk, I was struck by how thoroughly modern societies have woven invisible digital threads into every sinew of daily survival. As a technology columnist observing our hyper-connected era, I am increasingly concerned not by dramatic sci-fi scenarios of rogue machines, but by our quiet, voluntary surrender to pervasive technological dependence.",
