"Ultimately, ensuring that space exploration remains an engine of peaceful scientific discovery rather than an extension of earthly geopolitical conflict requires updating international space law for the twenty-first century—establishing enforceable debris-mitigation treaties, transparent rules for lunar resource governance, and inclusive multilateral cooperation."
