"JOURNALIST: What overarching framework do you advocate to overcome these medical blind spots in the twenty-first century?\nDR. OKAFOR: We must operationalize the 'One Health' paradigm—recognizing that human health, animal health, and planetary ecosystem integrity are inextricably bound together. Preventing the next pandemic requires protecting intact forests, regulating industrial livestock, strengthening primary healthcare and global genomic surveillance as shared public goods, and ensuring equitable access to medicines worldwide. True medical progress begins long before a patient enters a hospital ward."
