"texte": [
"Distinguished historians, educators, museum curators, and fellow citizens gathered at this National Forum on Historical Memory, how a society remembers its past is never a neutral exercise in archival cataloging; it is the crucible in which collective identity, civic values, and future aspirations are forged. As the French sociologist Maurice Halbwachs famously demonstrated in his pioneering theory of 'collective memory,' individual recollection is always anchored within shared social frameworks—public monuments, school curricula, commemorative holidays, and family narratives—that silently teach each generation who belongs to the national 'we' and whose suffering or contributions are remembered or forgotten.",
"Precisely because collective memory wields such immense unifying power, it is perpetually vulnerable to political manipulation. Throughout history, authoritarian regimes and nationalist mythmakers have curated selective, sanitized versions of the past—glorifying heroic victories while erasing colonial violence, minority persecution, or internal dissent. When history is reduced to self-congratulatory mythology, collective identity hardens into defensive tribalism incapable of self-criticism or reconciliation.",
"Conversely, mature democratic societies summon the moral courage to confront the full complexity of their historical inheritance—honoring genuine achievements of solidarity and emancipation while honestly reckoning with past injustices through transparent archives, inclusive memorials, and restorative dialogue.",
"Yet critical remembrance must never degenerate into paralyzing fatalism or hereditary guilt that traps present generations in endless vendettas; rather, honest historical reckoning liberates citizens from repeating inherited patterns of exclusion.",
"Therefore, my friends, let us cultivate a pluralistic, truthful, and empathetic culture of memory—one that gives voice to previously silenced histories and transforms shared remembrance into the ethical foundation of an inclusive, peaceful future."
