      "Unlike overt physical coercion—which announces itself unmistakably through force or legal threat—psychological manipulation succeeds precisely because its target believes they are acting entirely of their own free will. Reporting on behavioral economics and political persuasion as an investigative columnist over the past fifteen years, I have observed how techniques once confined to intimate interpersonal control or wartime propaganda have been systematized into ubiquitous commercial and digital architectures.",
