      "Inside a sprawling displacement camp in East Africa where tens of thousands of families shelter beneath sun-bleached tarpaulins after fleeing intersecting droughts and civil conflict, humanitarian logisticians recently faced an agonizing arithmetic: forced by severe international funding shortfalls to halve daily food rations, they had to decide which malnourished communities would receive dwindling supplies. Covering global emergencies as a humanitarian affairs columnist over the past decade, I have witnessed a sobering moral paradox: at the exact historical moment when climate shocks, protracted wars, and economic fragility have pushed global humanitarian needs to record highs, international solidarity is visibly fraying.",
