      "'I certainly do not deny that technology can be misused for destructive ends,' Dr. Lindholm replied, 'but isn't ethical progress itself often unlocked by material abundance? Historically, societies plagued by extreme scarcity rarely extended universal human rights or abolished forced labor; technological productivity created the material surplus that made moral expansion possible.'",
