"texte": [
"Fellow citizens, civic leaders, and members of this Constitutional Renewal Assembly, at the core of every democratic society lies a creative yet delicate tension: how to honor each individual's legitimate aspiration for personal autonomy, self-realization, and private property while safeguarding the collective interests, public goods, and ecological stability upon which everyone's freedom depends. Whenever public health mandates, progressive taxation, urban zoning rules, or environmental limits are proposed, debate swiftly polarizes into a false war between 'individual liberty' and 'collective coercion.' Yet if we examine the real fabric of human coexistence, we discover that unrestrained individual pursuit divorced from common responsibility ultimately destroys the very conditions of personal flourishing.",
"Economists and ecologists illustrate this paradox through the classic 'tragedy of the commons.' When every individual commuter insists on driving a private vehicle into a congested city center, or every fishing fleet maximizes its catch without collective quotas, each actor pursues an ostensibly rational self-interest—yet the aggregate outcome is gridlocked streets, toxic air, and collapsed fisheries that impoverish everyone alike.",
