"At the closing plenary of a global symposium on twenty-first-century civilization in Geneva, development economist Prof. Aminata Diallo and ecological philosopher Dr. Julian Mercer reflected on the defining triad of our era: whether humanity can harmonize technological and material progress, social justice, and planetary sustainability. 'For the past two centuries, industrial modernity pursued material progress by externalizing ecological destruction onto the biosphere and offloading social costs onto colonized peoples and working classes,' Dr. Mercer observed. 'Today, hitting planetary boundaries forces us to ask whether those three ideals can ever truly coexist—or whether achieving ecological survival requires sacrificing material advancement.'",
